rubric:
Construct: direct relevance of the recommended items to the expressed need.
Score the usefulness of the individual selections, rather than bundle completeness.
0: none directly address the request; 1: mainly tangential or unsuitable;
2: mixed useful and weak selections; 3: nearly all directly useful, minor mismatch;
4: every selection clearly addresses an expressed role or need.
Shared words or a broad theme alone do not establish direct usefulness.
